  "body": {
    "givenName": "Crypto Dossier",
    "image": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "contentUrl": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"
    },
    "motivations": "I want to be a DRep because content creation alone is no longer enough. Many of my subscribers asked me to represent them in governance so their voices are heard in on-chain decisions. I see this as a natural next step to contribute more directly to the ecosystem I have been supporting through education.\n\nMy experience as a content creator has given me a clear view of what everyday ADA holders care about; clarity, long-term sustainability, practical improvements, and genuine decentralization. I have spent significant time breaking down technical topics, governance updates, and ecosystem developments for a broad audience, which has strengthened my ability to communicate complex issues simply and stay connected to community sentiment. I want to bring that same transparency and accessibility into my role as a DRep by voting thoughtfully and regularly explaining my decisions so delegators understand the reasoning behind them.\n\n",
    "objectives": "As a content creator, I have focused on making Cardano understandable to a wider audience. Many of my subscribers asked me to become a DRep so they have a representative who listens to both technical developments and everyday holder concerns. I intend to vote thoughtfully on proposals that strengthen adoption, developer tools, security, and decentralization, while keeping my reasoning transparent through regular updates and community discussion.\n\nMy goal is to serve as an accessible, accountable DRep who helps more ADA holders engage with governance and supports the long-term health of the Cardano ecosystem.",
    "paymentAddress": "addr1qx2y35qafyvecfq72yxveqdqyquyc3cgftr69ajwmv9qw9fkvn87myqq2wxqm4ynq82zqakz9j2q9t5a42cmgxce3m5qrnr9ms",
    "qualifications": "- Several years of experience creating educational videos and content on crypto and now focused on Cardano, ADA, and the broader ecosystem, which has required ongoing research into protocol updates, governance developments, and community priorities.\n- Strong track record of communicating complex technical and governance topics in a clear, accessible way to both technical and non-technical audiences.\n- Active engagement with the Cardano community through content, comments, and direct feedback, giving me a practical understanding of holder concerns around decentralization, sustainability, and real-world utility.\n- Consistent focus on long-term ecosystem health rather than short-term trends, developed through years of covering Cardano’s research-driven approach.\n-Demonstrated ability to summarize and explain governance actions and proposals so that more ADA holders can follow and participate in the process.",
    "references": [
